  "interpretation": "The constellation test shows mixed results across frequency bands. The full TEP band (10-500 uHz) is NOT constellation-independent (GPS vs GLONASS p=8.2e-8, constellation_independent=False), indicating satellite-system-specific contributions in the broad band. However, the continuum band (25-100 uHz) IS constellation-independent (GPS vs GLONASS p=0.41, common > differential p=0.0012), ruling out satellite clock/orbit errors for the continuum component. The 8h solar tidal line is invariant to both troposphere and ephemeris treatment (<15% change), identifying it as gravitational rather than atmospheric or satellite-induced. Standard physics does not predict gravitational tidal lines in GNSS receiver clock bias. Atomic-atomic pairs show zero correlation in the full TEP band (BRUX-WTZR r=-0.04 at 638 km) while atomic-quartz pairs at similar distances show high correlation (BRUX-GRAS r=0.93 at 806 km), consistent with the TEP prediction that the atomic transition screens the field."
